<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carl Ulrich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1853–1933</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carl Ulrich was a German Social Democratic politician from Offenbach. After the revolution of 1918 he became the first President of the People's State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, governing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> until 1928 at the head of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a> coalition governments. He is regarded as the founder of democratic government in Hesse.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carl-ulrich.jpg" alt="Carl Ulrich" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carl_Ulrich_1870.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
